Calculate recall rates
For each participant and selected condition, the rate is the number of valid target-category positions recalled divided by the number presented. Recalling a position more than once does not increase this numerator. The figure averages participant rates, with bootstrap confidence intervals across participants.
A participant with no presented items in a category has an undefined rate for that category and is omitted from that summary. Thus the effective participant count can differ across bars. The CSV retains participant rows so you can inspect these differences.


