Optional paired contrasts
These calculations run only when you configure contrasts. paired_dataset chooses the dataset label; when unset, the first input is used. This section compares conditions/categories within that dataset, rather than testing observed versus simulated datasets against each other.
Each entry in comparisons is (label, left_condition, left_category, right_condition, right_category), using zero-based positions in your condition and category lists. For the supplied ordering, ("Mixed category difference", 0, 0, 0, 1) compares emotional with neutral recall in mixed lists. Only participants with finite scores on both sides are paired. The reported difference is left minus right.
An entry in contrast_of_contrasts contains a label and four (condition, category) pairs: it calculates (first − second) − (third − fourth) within participants present in all four cells. The output includes paired t/Wilcoxon tests and, for a contrast of contrasts with enough participants, a t interval. These tests are not adjusted for multiple comparisons; choose contrasts for your research question and inspect the participant counts.


